<article class="env-remark" id="00PY">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00PY">Remark <span data-tag="00PY">2.5.3.11</span>.</a> The theory of differential graded categories can be regarded as a special case of the more general theory of <em>$A_{\infty }$-categories</em> (see <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/MR1925734">MR1925734</a>]</span>). Definition <a data-tag="00PT" href="/tag/00PT">2.5.3.7</a> and Theorem <a data-tag="00PW" href="/tag/00PW">2.5.3.10</a> have been extended to the setting of $A_{\infty }$-categories by Faonte; we refer the reader to <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/MR3607208">MR3607208</a>]</span> for details. </p>
